  "claim": "The Borg parses a message stored at the last -more- prompt of the old level at the first keypress of the new level, before borg_update() moves borg.c. Both rune checks in borg_parse_aux() (the hit-by branch with runes tracked, and 'The rune of protection is broken!') then call square_iswarded(cave, borg.c) with the old level's position. When that position is outside the new level, a debug build aborts on square_istrap()'s bounds assertion and a release-style build reads outside the level's row array (AddressSanitizer: heap-buffer-overflow READ in square_istrap). Guarding both checks with square_in_bounds() removes the read; the rune list is still cleared, and inside-level and no-rune controls are byte-identical.",
  "full_tests": {
